  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: South Africa-India-United Kingdom Tri-lateral in Food and Nutrition Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO together with partner organisations, South Africa&apos;s Department of Science and Innovation (DSI) and India&apos;s Biotechnology Industry Research Assistance Council (BIRAC), have agreed to initiate a pilot project to identify and test opportunities to mobilise several near-term opportunities for trilateral cooperation to address enduring challenges in food and nutrition security, (with an initial focus on neglected, underutilised and indigenous species crops (NUS), in SA. The pilot is expected to start with a scoping phase in March 2024 that includes an expert mission from India to South Africa to set out potential approaches to initiate and implement the pilot in the remainder of the 2024/25 financial year. The pilot will serve as the implementation and learning phase to test joint knowledge sharing and innovation transfer interventions and provide recommendations for future collaborations in other sectors and geographies. The Expert Mission to SA in February/March will enable the joint development of the programme of work for the Pilot project.</narrative>
  </description>
